You may have it installed on the machine, but do you have your
head around all of the commands?  As I said, it's a question of
not having to learn everything at once.  If you don't know
anything, then you'll be able to compile a program and test it
quicker under Visual Studios.  (Of course, if you're already
familiar with the Unix toolkit, it would be foolish to ignore
it.)

> > One thing you might want to do fairly soon is to learn a
