> Yes. The thought of learning emacs or vi makes me want to cry (I
> looked at the emacs tutorial yesterday... what the hell kind of text
> editor has a tutrial fer crying out loud?

And decent program needs a tutorial.  You don't want to spend
all your time searching through hundreds of menus for the
simplest little action.  In practice, when I'm developing, I go
hours without touching the mouse---most importantly, without
moving my hands from the basic position on the keyboard.  That
alone is a major productivity enhancement.  And the power is
another, once you've learned it.

Also, if you're going to do any development at all, you should
learn touch typing as well.  It's simply a question of learning
your tools: and the editor and the keyboard are the principle
tools you'll have to cope with.

